    {
      "id": "EMD-04",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-embedding-common-rank",
      "title": "Why does one complex Weil space recover the original rank?",
      "hypotheses": "The L-representation V has finite rank a and is potentially semistable. The complex coefficient identification is compatible with the chosen embeddings. For the extension application use two potentially semistable models related by scalar extension.",
      "statement": "Each embedding part has dimension a, so the complex Weil space has dimension a. The equivariant surjection for an extension of coefficient fields is consequently an isomorphism with identical Weil characteristic polynomials.",
